\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Rise On Ag, Mining Strength; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2007\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes rose Friday, lifted by strength in the agricultural sector and in mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 202.45 points, or 0.99%, to end at 20,656.68.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 561.76 points, or 1.63%, to finish at 35,084.20.   \par \par \uc2 The agriculture subindex gained almost 8%.   \par \par \uc2 The biggest gainers were sugar producers, as investors watch to see whether the government will grant would-be ethanol producers some tax exemptions.   \par \par \uc2 Sugar producer Empresa Agroindustrial Casa Grande SAA (CASAGRC1.VL) gained 15% to end at 15.07 soles ($4.74).   \par \par \uc2 Banco de Credito said it had placed an overweight recommendation Casa Grande. The bank has a target price of PEN16.04 per share.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, investors once gain focused on zinc miner  \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA, (VOLB.VL) which gained 0.9% to PEN12.90.   \par \par \uc2 The head of research for Lima-based Centura SAB brokerage, Jorge Luis Rodriguez, said that the company's significant expansion plan coupled with strong metals prices is generating ongoing interest in Volcan.   \par \par \uc2 Moreover, according to Rodriguez, there is still upside potential. "We consider Volcan to be an attractive share," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) increased 2.5% to end at $25.00, while  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) rose 2.2% to end at $80.50.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly weaker at a midrate of PEN3.1785 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1780 to PEN3.1790.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1780, on a spread of PEN3.1770 to PEN3.1790.   \par \par \uc2 Depite Friday's weakness, the sol has been gaining ground recently as companies seek the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for tax-payment purposes.   \par \par \uc2 Consulting company Macroconsult said in a report that foreign companies have also been buying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for investments, with the expectation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and allow the sol to appreciate.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that some local banks and other financial institutions have also been reducing long U.S. dollar positions.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $35 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $2.37 billion.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 04-20-07 1634ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070420e34k0007a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
