\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Fall On Metals Decline; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2007\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes declined Thursday, dragged down by weakness in metal prices that hit a number of mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index fell 207.15 points, or 1.00%, to end at 20,454.23.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index decreased 226.34 points, or 0.65%, to finish at 34,522.44.   \par \par \uc2 "The stock market corrected today on profit taking after a long string of rises," a trader said.   \par \par \uc2 However, "one of the few shares to hold its own today was Volcan. There is still enormous interest in Volcan shares. There was lots of trading," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner  \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLB.VL) gained 6.3% to 13.00 soles ($4.09).   \par \par \uc2 According to the trader, the fact that Volcan is expected to report strong first-quarter earnings continues to garner interest.   \par \par \uc2 Many other mining companies fell, though.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) declined 2.4% to end at $24.40, while  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) fell 1.5% to end at $78.80 on weaker copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 Precious and base metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) ended 1.5% lower at PEN105.45 on weaker gold prices.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol Thursday ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN3.1780 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1770 to PEN3.1790, the official said.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1790 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1780 to PEN3.1800.   \par \par \uc2 The sol has been gaining ground recently as companies seek the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for tax payment purposes, and as foreign investors seek soles to invest in the stock market.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $50 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $150 million Tuesday, the largest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year, and $115 million Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-19-07 1632ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070419e34j0007p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
