\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Up 0.95% To New Record High   \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2007\par 22:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes powered to a new record high Wednesday in heavy volumes as investors continue to pour into the stock market.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 193.59 points, or 0.95%, to end at 20,661.38.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 442.05 points, or 1.29%, to finish at 33,748.78.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market indexes have now hit records for 16 out of the last 17 sessions, with the exception of a slight decline last Wednesday, April 11.   \par \par \uc2 "There was a great deal of trading volume today due to enthusiasm. The number of trades was double what it usually is. There is a lot of interest in mining shares and in sugar producers," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 According to the trader, the indexes were stronger earlier in the session but fell back slightly due to profit-taking, in particular among the sugar producers.   \par \par \uc2 Mining shares, meanwhile, continued to garner strong interest.   \par \par \uc2 "The metals prices are high and these companies are about to publish their earnings reports and they are expected to be good," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Heavily-traded zinc miner  \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLB.VL) gained 5.4% to 12.23 soles ($3.84) on expectations the company will post strong first-quarter earnings.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 0.6% to end at $25.00, while miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) ended 0.5% higher at PEN107.00 on stronger gold prices.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) gained 1.0% to end at $52.70.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol Wednesday ended slightly weaker at a midrate of PEN3.1790 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1780 to PEN3.1800.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1780 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1770 to PEN3.1790.   \par \par \uc2 The sol has been gaining ground recently as companies seek the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for tax payment purposes.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $115 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $150 million Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Deutsche Bank said in a report Wednesday that it "remains bullish" on the sol due to a fundamental view that Peru's strong external position is to remain in place.   \par \par \uc2 The bank added that the sol is around 5% undervalued in real terms and that it should continue to gradually trend toward a PEN3.15 to the U.S. dollar target level.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-18-07 1633ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070418e34i00076\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
