\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Climbs 2.64% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2007\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes rose again to new record-closing highs Monday, as strong investor confidence continued to lift a wide range of company shares.   \par \par \uc2 "We are seeing a lot of new entrants in the market, and cash flowing in from outside of Peru," said one trader, pointing to increased confidence on the part of investors.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 512.04 points, or 2.64%, to end at 19,924.33.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 728.12 points, or 2.23%, to finish at 33,425.54.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market indexes have now hit new records for 15 consecutive sessions, except for a slight decline last Wednesday. So far this year, the general index is up some 55%, after gaining 168% last year.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 1.3% to end at $24.27.   \par \par \uc2 Miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) ended 5.6% higher at 103.70 soles ($32.61).   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 ,(PCU) however, went the other way, falling 0.4% to end at $78.10.   \par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley on Monday downgraded Southern Copper's shares, citing "a trading opportunity given their currently rich valuation and our expectations for a negative 1Q07 earnings surprise. We are maintaining our EPS estimates for the year and our $58 price target."   \par \par \uc2 Sugar producers also continued to gain, as the government is studying giving tax breaks for using ethanol as a fuel.   \par \par \uc2 Sugar producer Empresa Agroindustrial Casa Grande SAA (CASAGRC1.VL) rose 12% to PEN14.80.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN3.1795 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1790 to PEN3.1800.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1805 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1800 to PEN3.1810.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $95 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Deutsche Bank said in a report Monday that Peru has a largely current account and commodity driven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "that is benefiting from terms-of-trade gains and productivity growth."   \par \par \uc2 It added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was undervalued by 6% or more, and that there is a large excess supply of dollars in the economy that can sustain appreciation pressures.   \par \par \uc2 "The scope for nominal appreciation is, however, constrained by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will be gradual," it added.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-16-07 1650ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070416e34g00072\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
