\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Up 2.74% To End At Record High   \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2007\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes rose to a new record high Tuesday, for the 12th consecutive session, with mining companies once again leading the gains.   \par \par \uc2 "The stock exchange is unstoppable. There is a strong inflow of cash, in particular from mutual funds as people look to invest. There are also new, local investors who are investing directly. The bourse has attracted a lot of attention. Shares keep climbing," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 504.96 points, or 2.74%, to end at 18,946.15.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 1,041.20 points, or 3.35%, to finish at 32,092.94.   \par \par \uc2 Rising metals prices continued to boost mining shares on the Lima Stock Exchange on Tuesday, as the mining subindex rose 2.91%.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) benefited from investor optimism and strong copper prices, gaining 7.0% to end at $24.00.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rose 1.3% to end at $78.00.   \par \par \uc2 Heavily traded zinc miner  \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 2.7% to end at 10.68 soles ($3.36) on positive sentiment about the company's first-quarter earnings.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc-lead miner  \uc2 Compania Minera Atacocha SA\uc2 's (ATACOC1.VL) investment share increased 8.3% to end at PEN22.20.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) gained 1.4% to end at $51.50.   \par \par \uc2 Regulatory agency Conasev noted Tuesday in a report that the general index rose 33.1% in the first quarter, while the selective index gained 29.6%.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol Tuesday ended unchanged at a midrate of PEN3.1815 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1810 to PEN3.1820.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $20 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-10-07 1638ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070410e34a0006q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
