\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 1.65% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2007\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes climbed to record highs Monday, for the 11th consecutive session, again lifted by strength in mining companies and by interest in various smaller companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 299.88 points, or 1.65%, to end at 18,441.19.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 440.32 points, or 1.44%, to finish at 31,051.74.   \par \par \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) was 1.0% higher at 100.00 soles ($31.43), on stronger gold prices.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 2.4% to end at $22.43, while  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rose 2.5% to end at $77.00.   \par \par \uc2 Monday's market was also boosted by Empresa Siderurgica del Peru SAA, or  \uc2 Siderperu\uc2  (SIDERC1), one trader said. The share gained 7.4% to PEN2.60.   \par \par \uc2 "The company is planning a public share offer and investors are speculating that the price might be around $1.00 so there is a lot of interest in the share right now," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Brazilian long steel maker Gerdau (GGB) bought a controlling stake in  \uc2 Siderperu\uc2  last year.   \par \par \uc2 The trader also pointed to sugar producers such as Empresa Agroindustrial Tuman SAA (TUMANC1.VL), which gained 11.1% to PEN7.00 over the course of the session.   \par \par \uc2 Sugar producers have caught investor interest in recent months due to a growing interest in ethanol production.   \par \par \uc2 "Sugar producers are going to be the share of the year," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Lima-based brokerage Centura SAB said in a report that it expected the bourse to show "relatively high activity" this week, as investors look forward to the release of strong first-quarter earnings.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market was closed Thursday and Friday for Easter Week holidays.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol Monday ended slightly weaker at a midrate of PEN3.1815 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1810 to PEN3.1820.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1810 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1800 to PEN3.1820.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $45 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Like the stock market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was closed Thursday and Friday due to holiday observance.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-09-07 1633ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070409e3490004v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
