\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 1.28% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2007\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes climbed to new record highs Wednesday for the tenth consecutive day, lifted by strength in base metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 229.48 points, or 1.28%, to end at 18,141.31.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 320.26 points, or 1.06%, to finish at 30,611.42.   \par \par \uc2 "Basically what moved today's market was zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) after the company held its annual board meeting Tuesday," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Volcan was heavily traded in the session and gained 2.1% to 10.40 soles ($3.27).   \par \par \uc2 According to the trader, Volcan said that it fared well in the first quarter and also said it planned to distribute dividends. Company officials weren't available to confirm the first-quarter results or the dividend distribution.   \par \par \uc2 "Volcan is a company that is doing well. If the zinc prices stay high, it will continue making money," said the trader.   \par \par \uc2 Volcan and other miners were also supported by solid metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) was 1.2% higher at PEN99.00, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 0.2% to end at $21.90.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) continued to gain, rising 2.2% to end at $50.91.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended unchanged Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.1810 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1800 to PEN3.1820.   \par \par \uc2 The sol has remained strong due to demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from mining companies to make tax payments.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $70 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Both the stock market and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed Thursday and Friday for Easter week holidays.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 04-04-07 1655ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070404e3440007r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
