\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 1.53% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock index climbed to another record high Thursday, its sixth consecutive day of gains, boosted mainly by rising metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 256.26 points, or 1.53%, to end at 17,019.05 - a new record.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 476.10 points, or 1.70%, to finish at 28,493.42.   \par \par \uc2 "Today's rise is primarily linked to mining shares. Base metals prices recovered in London, in particular copper and zinc. This led to a strong rise in shares like Volcan and Milpo," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Heavily traded Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 2.2% to 9.50 soles ($2.98) while base metals miner  \uc2 Compania Minera Milpo\uc2  SAA (MILPOC1) increased a strong 8.0% to PEN13.50.   \par \par \uc2 The trader also pointed to a strong rise in base metals miner Compania Minera  \uc2 San Ignacio de Morococha\uc2  SA (MOROCOI1.VL), which gained 8.4% to end at PEN7.75.   \par \par \uc2 Other miners also posted good gains.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 3.2% to end at $19.40.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) rose 0.7% at PEN94.00.   \par \par \uc2 Another miner, Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL), which runs Peru's only tin mine, ended 1.1% higher at PEN9.10.   \par \par \uc2 The electricity sector also helped boost the indexes Thursday, the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Thursday at a midrate of PEN3.1835 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1830 to PEN3.1840.   \par \par \uc2 The sol had ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1845 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1840 to PEN3.1850.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $10 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to help build international reserves.   \par \par \uc2 So far in March the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $560 million.   \par \par \uc2 In a report Peru's Banco de Credito said it expects demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain strong during the current annual corporate income tax payment period, which started this week.   \par \par \uc2 It noted that the booming economy will boost those corporate tax payments to some 4.0 billion soles ($1.26 billion) this year, while from 1998 to 2004 the payments were some PEN600 million a year.   \par \par \uc2 "We expect there will be an excess offer of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , produced by the demand for soles for the tax payment period, which should lead the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it added in the report released late Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 03-29-07 1636ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070329e33t0009j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
