\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 1.15% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock index climbed to another record high Wednesday, as mining companies and those in the industrial sector again posted good gains.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 190.22 points, or 1.15%, to end at 16,762.79, a new record.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 264.47 points, or 0.95%, to finish at 28,017.32.   \par \par \uc2 Mining shares continue to garner interest Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "Their prices are good and many companies are expanding their production so investors have high expectations," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 1.6% to end at $18.80, while  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) rose 0.2% to end at $71.65.   \par \par \uc2 Another miner, Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL), continued to rise, despite weakness in tin prices. Minsur, which runs Peru's only tin mine, ended 0.6% higher at 9.00 soles ($2.83).   \par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of liquidity in the market right now and the economic projections are extremely encouraging. After the tremendous boom in mining shares the industrial shares have begun to gain strongly," the trader added.   \par \par \uc2 Peru's economy is expected to expand by more than 7.0% this year.   \par \par \uc2 One big gainer, for example, in Wednesday's market was  \uc2 Exsa SA\uc2  (EXSAC1), a company that makes explosives used primarily in mining. The share gained 15.2% to PEN3.11.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly weaker at a midrate of PEN3.1845 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1840 to PEN3.1850.   \par \par \uc2 The sol had ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1830 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1820 to PEN3.1840.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 So far in March the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $550 million.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    \par  -0- \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-28-07 1646ET ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070328e33s0008t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
