\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Ends Up 0.62% To Record High  \b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock index climbed to another new record high Tuesday, as mining companies, and some companies in the agriculture sector, led the increase.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 102.09 points, or 0.62%, to end at 16,572.57 - a new record.  \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index rose 145.79 points, or 0.53%, to finish at 27,752.85.  \par \par \uc2 Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 1.1% to end at $18.50, while copper miner Southern Copper Corp.(PCU) rose 0.9% to end at $71.50.  \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner Compania de Minas Buenaventura SAA (BVN) gained 0.6% to end at 94.62 soles ($29.73).  \par \par \uc2 Another miner, Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL), continued to rise, as tin prices hit a record high. Minsur, which runs Peru's only tin mine, ended 0.6% higher at PEN8.95.  \par \par \uc2 "The outlook in the mining sector is very encouraging," said one market analyst.  \par \par \uc2 Among other companies, Gloria SA (GLORIAI1.VL) fared well in the session, rising 14.1% to PEN3.65. Gloria produces milk products.  \par \par \uc2 "To a great extent what we have seen today is a response to rising confidence in the local economy," one analyst said.  \par \par \uc2 The Lima Chamber of Commerce, which Tuesday lifted its forecast for growth in Peru's gross domestic product for 2007 to a 7.4% expansion, also said that the mining and hydrocarbons sector should expand 3.4% this year.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly weaker at a midrate of PEN3.1830 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1820 to PEN3.1840.  \par \par \uc2 The sol had ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1820 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1810 to PEN3.1830.  \par \par \uc2 An annual income tax payment period started Tuesday, which has increased demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $60 million.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to help build international reserves.  \par \par \uc2 So far in March the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $550 million.  \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 03-27-07 1652ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070327e33r0008j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
