\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Ends Up 0.81% To Record High  \b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock index rose to another record high Monday, propelled by gains in a wide range of industrial shares and by strong metals prices that lifted mining companies.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 131.62 points, or 0.81%, to end at 16,470.48, a new record.  \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index rose 81.94 points, or 0.30%, to finish at 27,607.06.  \par \par \uc2 "The domestic market is growing, and investors are banking on the fact that it is going to keep on growing," one trader said. "This is generating interest in shares from the industrial sector, agriculture shares and shares related to service companies like energy distributor Hidrandina."  \par \par \uc2 The Empresa Regional de Servicio Publico de Electricidad Electro Norte Media S.A., or Hidrandina, (HIDRA2C1.VL) continued to be one of the biggest gainers in Monday's market, rising 14.9% to 0.85 sol ($0.27).  \par \par \uc2 The company rose 12.3% on Thursday and 15.6% on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Another key gainer in Monday's market was sugar producer Empresa Agroindustrial Pomalca SAA (POMALCC1.VL), which increased 7.7% to PEN0.70.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of interest in companies like Pomalca right now because of the potential to produce ethanol," said the trader.  \par \par \uc2 Miners, which have led the market higher in recent years, again posted solid gains.  \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Southern Copper Corp.(PCU) rose 1.4% to end at $71.50, while Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 1.1% to end at $18.30, both gaining on stronger prices for the red metal.  \par \par \uc2 Another miner, Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL), gained 0.6% to end at PEN8.90, on a rise in tin prices.  \par \par \uc2 Minsur runs Peru's only tin mine.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, Lima Stock Exchange President Carmela de Marrou was quoted by newspaper Gestion Monday as saying that the stock market could rise by some 40% this year.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN3.1820 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1810 to PEN3.1830.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at at a midrate of PEN3.1835 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1830 to PEN3.1840.  \par \par \uc2 A report by Scotiabank noted that Friday's close had been the strongest for the sol so far this year and the best showing for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early 1999.  \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $100 million.  \par \par \uc2 A monthly tax payment period, which normally increases appreciation pressures on the sol, will end Monday. However, an annual income tax payment period starts on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to help build international reserves.  \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 26-03-07 2045GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070326e33q0016x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
