\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Ends Up 0.45% To Record High  \b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 21:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Strength in a wide range of shares lifted Peru's main stock index to another record high Friday.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 73.07 points, or 0.45%, to end at 16,338.86, a new record.  \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index rose 122.85 points, or 0.45%, to finish at 27,525.12.  \par \par \uc2 "Some small industrial shares helped boost the index today. There is a huge amount of money in the market right now and investors are looking for opportunities. These are companies that showed strong earnings in 2006," said one trader.  \par \par \uc2 The top gainer for a second day was energy distributor Empresa Regional de Servicio Publico de Electricidad Electro Norte Media S.A. or Hidrandina. (HIDRA2C1.VL)  \par \par \uc2 That share has been rising due to strong profits in 2006 and a positive future outlook.  \par \par \uc2 Hidrandina gained 15.6% to end at 0.74 of a sol ($0.23) on Friday. The company rose 12.3% on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Blue chips also turned in a good performance.  \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company Credicorp Ltd. (BAP) rose 0.2% to end at $49.10.  \par \par \uc2 Credicorp's main holding is Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito, which has gained favor as the Andean nation's economy continues to expand strongly.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Standard & Poor's Ratings Services raised its Banking Industry Country Risk Assessment on Peru, reflecting, it said, "the improved economic environment in Peru and its beneficial impact on the creditworthiness of banks operating in the country ..."  \par \par \uc2 Some miners also showed good strength Friday, despite general weakness in metals prices.  \par \par \uc2 Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 1.6% to end at $18.30.  \par \par \uc2 Zinc, silver and lead miner Sociedad Minera El Brocal SAA (BROCALC1.VL) rose again, ending 2.2% higher at PEN46.00.  \par \par \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura SAA (BVN) closed 0.5% higher at PEN94.00.  \par \par \uc2 Going the other way was heavy equipment supplier Ferreyros SAA, (FERREYC1.VL) which fell 2.4% to end at PEN5.75.  \par \par \uc2 Banco de Credito said Friday it had placed an "underweight" recommendation on Ferreyros, saying an analysis had arrived at a "fundamental" share price of PEN5.13.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN3.1835 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1830 to PEN3.1840.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1855 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1850 to PEN3.1860.  \par \par \uc2 That followed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $70 million.  \par \par \uc2 A current monthly tax payment period, which normally increases appreciation pressures on the sol, will end on March 26.  \par \par \uc2 "However, it is expected that the appreciation of the sol could increase from March 27, when an (annual) income tax payment period starts," economic consulting firm Macroconsult said in a report Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Peru's sol has been strengthening in recent years, in part due to the Andean nation's strong external accounts.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to help build international reserves.  \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, 