\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Ends At Record High; Sol Strengthens  \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2007\par 22:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock index ended at a record high Thursday, as stronger mineral prices again lifted mining company shares.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index increased 37.20 points, or 0.26%, to end at 14,586.89.  \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index gained 153.64 points, or 0.63%, to finish at 24,648.43.  \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp. (PCU) increased 0.6% to end at $68.00, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 3.9% to end at $14.85 as copper prices increased.  \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 0.4% to end at 7.60 soles ($2.38) on stronger zinc prices.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $50 million.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger Thursday at a midrate of PEN3.1870 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1860 to PEN3.1880.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1895 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1890 to PEN3.1900.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Transaction volumes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market totaled $122.5 million Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 02-15-07 1635ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument