\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Weakens A Bit  \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2007\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes dropped Friday, weighed down by weakness in metal prices.  \par \par \uc2 According to results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index fell 110.37 points, or 0.81%, to end at 13,563.93, while the selective blue chip index decreased 286.53 points, or 1.25%, to finish at 22,717.93.  \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.(PCU) dropped 1.7% to end at $62.90 on weaker copper prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) lost 1.1% at end at $13.85.  \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 2.7% to end at 7.15 soles ($2.24) as zinc prices eased.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol weakened slightly Friday, ending at a midrate of PEN3.1960 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1950 to PEN3.1970.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1955 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1950 to PEN3.1960.  \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the week. So far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased some $610 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Consulting firm Macroconsult said in a report Friday that the strengthening trend of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due mainly to the sale of U.S. dollars by mining companies seeking soles before the start of the Feb. 9 tax payment period.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 02-02-07 1616ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00