\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Weakens A Bit  \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2007\par 21:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's stock market indexes gained Monday as stronger metals prices helped lift mining company shares.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index gained 152.59 points, or 1.15%, to end at 13,429.25. The selective blue chip index rose 385.98 points, or 1.72%, to finish at 22,782.70.  \par \par \uc2 Among the mining companies that gained, copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 1.1% to end at $14.05 as copper prices gained.  \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Southern Copper Corp. (PCU) increased 0.2% to end at $55.70.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $30 million.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves. So far in January the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $610 million.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended weaker Monday at a midrate of PEN3.1900 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1890 to PEN3.1910.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1880 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1870 to PEN3.1890.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 01-22-07 1555ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM000000200701