\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Mixed; Sol Stronger  \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2007\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's stock indexes ended mixed Thursday as various blue-chip shares moved in opposite directions.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index fell 44.51 points, or 0.34%, to end at 13,091.16, while the selective blue-chip index rose 65.92 points, or 0.30%, to finish at 22,043.83.  \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company Credicorp Ltd. (BAP) rose 0.6% to end at $42.20, while precious metals miner Compania de Minas Buenaventura SAA (BVN) gained 1.9% to 86.50 soles. ($27.13)  \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) advanced 1.4% to $13.70.  \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL), on the other hand, fell 0.3% to PEN7.25 as zinc prices weakened.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $70 million.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN3.1865 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1860 to PEN3.1870.  \par \par \uc2 The sol finished the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1875 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1870 to PEN3.1880.  \par \par \uc2 Banco de Credito said in a report Thursday that demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for tax payment purposes will continue until Jan. 25.  \par \par \uc2 "For the following week the exchange rate will continue its (appreciating) trend seen in the last few days," it said. "Dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only reduce volatility in the exchange rate, which will move between PEN3.185 per dollar to PEN3.189 per dollar."  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221-7050 [ 01-18-07 1616ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070118e31i0006p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
