\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Continue Decline; Sol Stronger  \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2007\par 21:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes continued to decline Monday, as a number of mining companies fell due to weaker mineral prices.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index fell 194.27 points, or 1.54%, to end at 12,450.02, while the selective blue-chip index weakened 397.15 points, or 1.86%, to finish at 20,972.83.  \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) continued to slide, dropping 1.6% to end at $12.40 on a decline in copper prices.  \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 4.5% to end at 7.40 soles ($2.32) as zinc prices eased.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $60 million at an average of PEN3.1912 to the U.S. dollar, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger Monday at a midrate of PEN3.1915 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1910 to PEN3.1920.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1925 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1920 to PEN3.1930.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 01-08-07 1548ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM0000002007