\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Decline Again; Sol Weakens A Bit  \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2007\par 21:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes declined again Friday, as weaker mineral prices continued to drag down mining company shares.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index fell 188.44 points, or 1.47%, to end at 12,630.56, while the selective blue chip index weakened 439.62 points, or 2.02%, to finish at 21,334.63.  \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) lost 6.0% to end at $12.60 on a sharp decline in copper prices.  \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner Compania de Minas Buenaventura SAA (BVN) declined 2.0% to end at 84.80 soles ($26.59) as gold prices continued to ease.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $10 million at an average of PEN3.1929 to the U.S. dollar, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly weaker Friday at a midrate of PEN3.1925 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1920 to PEN3.1930.  \par \par \uc2 The sol had ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1920 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1910 to PEN3.1930.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy a total of $95 million during the week.  \par \par \uc2 Consulting firm Macroconsult said in a report Friday that demand for the sol has grown in part due to pension fund administrators and foreign buyers, drawn by strong economic growth and by increased investments in Peru's stock market.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow