\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Gains Strength  \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2006\par 21:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's stock market indexes ended lower Tuesday as some key blue chip shares declined.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index fell 30.89 points, or 0.29%, to end at 10,685.26. The selective blue chip index declined 62.77 points, or 0.34%, to finish at 18,444.39.  \par \par \uc2 Miner Compania de Minas Buenaventura SAA (BVN) lost 0.3% to end at 82.01 soles ($25.52).  \par \par \uc2 UBS on Tuesday cut EPS estimates for Buenaventura to $3.76 in 2007, from previous $4.00. The firm also cuts 2008 estimate to $2.48/share from a previous $2.75, citing lower forecasts for gold prices.  \par \par \uc2 Refineria La Pampilla SA lost 10.7% to end at PEN29.30 in heavy trade.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended slightly stronger Tuesday, ending at a midrate of PEN3.2140 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.2110 to PEN3.2170.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.2145 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2090 to PEN3.2200.  \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $70 million over the course of the session. During the month of October the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase a total of $696.1 million.  \par \par \uc2 -Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 10-31-06 1553ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020061031e2av0006t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
