\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Genl Stock Index Ends At Record High; Sol Weakens  \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2006\par 22:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Wednesday as a number of blue-chip shares gained.  \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 72.89 points, or 0.78%, to 9,382.30, a record high.  \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 132.57 points, or 0.81%, to end at 16,548.88.  \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company Credicorp Ltd. (BAP) rose 1.0% to $31.50. The company will report second-quarter financial results Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner Compania de Minas Buenaventura SAA (BVN) increased 0.8% to end at 96.75 soles ($29.93) on weakness in gold prices.  \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 2.0% to end at PEN5.20 as zinc prices gained, while tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) gained 1.1% to end at PEN4.65 on a rise in tin prices.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, on Wednesday, the free-floating sol ended a bit weaker at a midrate of PEN3.2315 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.2310-PEN3.2320.  \par \par \uc2 The sol closed the previous trading session at a midrate of PEN3.2300 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2290-PEN3.2310, reaching its strongest level since January 1999.  \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $111.5 million in open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease appreciation pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol.  \par \par \uc2 The demand for soles came Wednesday from mining companies who need the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay taxes as well as from other sectors, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows Tuesday's record-high one-day purchase of $213 million.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 08-09-06 1638ET ]  \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020060809e2890003o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
