\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  More As Sol Strengthens  \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2006\par 16:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  may continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to limit gains in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol, banks said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $500,000 Wednesday, the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in about three months, as the sol appreciates amid strong economic growth. Peru's gross domestic product expanded 10.7% in March, the government's statistics agency said this week.  \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said that some banks were unloading long positions in U.S. dollars, at a time when greenbacks continue to flow into the country, especially from mining companies.  \par \par \uc2 Banco Wiese Sudameris said in a market report that the government's Banco de la Nacion has also bought some $200 million during the last weeks, aiming to stem the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It added that if in the coming days the appreciation continues, due to tax payment reasons and the solid economic fundamentals, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  participation in the market will have an important signaling effect.  \par \par \uc2 "We can't rule out that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short term, in the measure that Banco de la Nacion purchases aren't sufficient to balance the market," Banco Wiese Sudameris added.  \par \par \uc2 It noted that the sol has appreciated some 4.6% so far this year, and some 3% since the April 9 general elections.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the free-floating sol ended at a midrate of PEN3.2595 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In a separate report, Banco de Credito said that the sol could continue within a range of PEN3.2450 to PEN3.2700 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The final range will depend on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains its position in the exchange market with small \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  accompanying the appreciation while moderating any abrupt declines, or if it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with larger amounts to try to alter the direction guided by the fundamentals," Banco de Credito added.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acting-President Oscar Dancourt said in a television interview this week that it has sufficient international reserves - at some $14.5 billion - to ward off any speculative attacks on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 18-05-06 1426GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060518e25i000w9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
