\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Sol Weakens; Stocks Gain Ground   \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2006\par 21:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol ended weaker against the dollar Wednesday, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold $15.5 million.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended at a midrate of PEN3.4445 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4440-PEN3.4450.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous trading session at a midrate of PEN3.4425 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4420-PEN3.4430.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling U.S. dollars in recent trading sessions, aiming to ease volatility tied to concerns about the upcoming elections. On Monday it sold a one-day record of $104.5 million, while on Tuesday it sold another $59.5 million.   \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.60% on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Peru's main stock indexes rose Wednesday as various stocks that had sold off in recent sessions began to regain ground.   \par \par \uc2 Preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange show that the stock market's broad general index rose 29.01 points, or 0.62%, to end at 4680.81, while the selective blue chip index increased 70.69 points, or 0.95%, to close at 7511.22.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Southern Copper Corp. (PCU) rose 0.7% to end at $70.50, while beverage producer Union de Cervecerias Peruanas Backus & Johnston SAA (BACKUSI.VL) rose 2.8% to end at 1.87 soles. ($0.54)   \par \par \uc2 Telefonica SA (TEF) increased 0.7% to end at $47.50, following the direction of its New York-traded American Depositary Receipt.   \par 