\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Peru's Stocks Drop On Political Concerns; Sol Unchanged  \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2006\par 21:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Jan 10, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 Concerns that a left-wing nationalist presidential candidate could take the lead in opinion polls before April's elections helped push Peru's main stock indexes lower on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange show that the stock market's broad general index fell 114.40 points, or 2.40%, to end at 4647.34, while the selective blue chip index lost 203.74 points, or 2.67%, to close at 7430.24.  \par \par \uc2 Peru's largest cement producer, Cementos Lima SA (CEMLIMI1.VL), lost 2.7% to end at 3.56 soles ($1.03).  \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner Compania de Minas Buenaventura SAA (BVN) lost 0.9% to end at PEN105.50 in heavy trade.  \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) lost 3.0% to end at $3.83, while zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 4.7%, ending at PEN1.02 ($0.30).  \par \par \uc2 Presidential candidate Ollanta Humala, who has said he would introduce higher taxes on mining company profits, has gained in popularity and observers are watching to see if new polls expected to be released shortly show him to be the new front-runner.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Peru's sol ended unchanged Tuesday after the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell $59.5 million.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended Tuesday at a midrate of PEN3.4425 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4420-PEN3.4430.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a one-day record of $104.5 million on Monday to ease volatility, helping support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.59% on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 -Robert Kozak; Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 01-10-06 1536ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060110e21a009rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
