\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Ctrl Bk May Lift Reference Interest Rate - Banks  \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2006\par 18:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--The Central Reserve Bank of Peru's board of directors may opt to increase the key reference rate for open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it holds its first meeting of the year on Thursday, economists said.  \par \par \uc2 They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could raise the key reference rate to 3.50% from 3.25% in an attempt to ward off volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 "It would mainly be aimed at controlling volatility," said Guillermo Diaz, chief economist at Banco Wiese Sudameris.  \par \par \uc2 At a press conference Tuesday, Diaz said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lift the key reference rate by 75 basis points in the first part of this year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last raised the reference rate to 3.25% in December, the first increase since October 2004, aiming to reduce volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and make speculation more costly.  \par \par \uc2 Economists say that rising interest rates in the U.S. as well as higher levels of political uncertainty before April's election in Peru are two factors that have undermined the stability of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Given that episodes of exchange-rate volatility have continued, we can't rule out that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could increase its reference rate," the economic studies service of BBVA Banco Continental said in a report released late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 In December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by selling U.S. dollar directly or by offering certificates indexed to the U.S. dollar valued at $644 million, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  calls an "unprecedented" amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation rate the lowest in the region, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has little need to increase interest rates to cool price pressures. The consumer price index rose by only 1.49% in 2005, touching the bottom end of the target range set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to keep consumer inflation within a one percentage point range above or below a midpoint of 2.5% into the indefinite future.  \par \par \uc2 In 2004 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased its reference rate twice, in August and in October, as inflation temporarily exceeded the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range as a result of various supply shocks.  \par \par \uc2 In 2002, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to a system of inflation targeting as its main monetary tool.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 03-01-06 1751GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060103e213000mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
