\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Peru Sol Strengthens, Stock Indexes Decline  \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2005\par 21:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Dec 13, 2005 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 Peru's sol strengthened Tuesday, as the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling U.S. dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended at a midrate of PEN3.4355 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4350-PEN3.4360.  \par \par \uc2 The sol closed the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.4405 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.4400-PEN3.4410.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $3 million Tuesday, after selling $80.5 million the previous day.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weakening on dollar buying by private pension funds, increased U.S. interest rates and on nervousness over the coming elections, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.43% Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Peru's stock market weakened Tuesday as blue chip financial institution Credicorp Ltd. (BAP) fell sharply.  \par \par \uc2 The stock market's broad general index lost 31.10 points, or 0.60%, to end at 5168.72, while the selective blue chip index fell 39.39 points, or 0.47%, to close at 8340.41.  \par \par \uc2 Credicorp, owner of Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito, fell 4.0% to end at $26.82.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, UBS Investment Research cut its risk exposure to Peru to zero in its model portfolio, selling its holdings of Credicorp.  \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Southern Copper Corp.(PCU) went the other way, rising 2.9% to end at $71.00 on stronger copper prices.  \par \par \uc2