\par\par \b \uc2 = Peru Markets Rattled By Rise Of Nationalist Pres Hopeful  \b0\par\par\uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2005\par 21:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Dec 13, 2005 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Robert Kozak\par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The rapid rise in popularity of nationalist presidential candidate Ollanta Humala has started to rattle Peru's financial markets, with observers expecting more turbulence ahead of the April elections.  \par \par \uc2 While opinion polls still show the ex-army officer lagging behind in his attempt to become president, with former Congresswoman Lourdes Flores in the lead, Humala appears to be closing the gap.  \par \par \uc2 A survey by pollster Apoyo Opinion y Mercado SA, published Sunday in newspaper El Comercio, showed the right of center Lourdes with 25% support, down from 28% in November. But public support for populist Humala rose to 22%, a sharp increase from 11% in the previous month and from just 2% in December 2004.  \par \par \uc2 That was enough to trigger a sell-off in Peruvian soles, leading the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday and sell a $80.5 million in an attempt to ease pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the sol weakened anyway, closing Monday at a midrate of PEN3.4405 to the dollar compared with a midrate of PEN3.4130 to the dollar in the previous session. In midday trade Tuesday, the sol was almost unchanged at a midrate of 3.4425 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers expect the uncertainty surrounding Humala's policies to weaken confidence in the Andean nation. Humala, 43, has tapped into widespread dissatisfaction among Peru's poor with his self-proclaimed goal of "defending national interests against globalization."  \par \par \uc2 In a research report, Credit Suisse First Boston economist Carola Sandy said: "We think that, in coming months, voters' support for Humala could continue to increase, which would result in volatility of Peruvian asset prices."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars since mid-October as the sol has weakened due to large dollar purchases by local pension funds, rising U.S. interest rates and political uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 That's in contrast to its pattern of buying dollars in recent years to rein in the sol, which has been boosted by Peru's expanding trade surplus.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most recent dollar sales came about despite strong seasonal demand for soles in December, and the sale of some PEN811 million in sol-denominated local debt last Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Although the government was able to successfully place the bonds in the local market, the amount issued was below the PEN930 million the government had originally said it would offer. Analysts said that was due partly to nervousness over the elections and weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which reduced demand for the treasury paper.  \par \par \uc2 "We estimate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility will continue through this week, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be ready to sell dollars to cut off any speculative attacks against the sol," BBVA Banco Continental said in a report.  \par \par \uc2 It added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also likely to tighten liquidity, leaving the interbank rate above the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reference rate of 3.25%. The interbank rate closed Monday at 3.42%.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted its key reference rate from 3.0%, the first increase since October 2004, saying it wanted to reduce volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to make speculative movements more costly.  \par \par \uc2 The rising uncertainty tied to Humala's higher popularity ratings could also lead to jitters in the equity market.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, UBS Investment Research cut its risk exposure to Peru to zero in its model portfolio, selling its holdings of Credicorp Ltd. (BAP), owner of Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.  \par \par \uc2 "Whilst we think Humala's presidential chances are slim, they are nevertheless real, and we do not think the equity market has taken this on-board," said UBS. "Hence, we see short-term downside as the market prices in at least the possibility of a Humala victory."  \par \par \uc2 Around noon Tuesday, Credicorp's American Depository Receipts were trading down a sharp 4.1% at $26.96.  \par \par \uc2 The newly elected president will assume office in July for a five-year term.  \par \par \uc2 President Alejandro Toledo can't run for office again in 2006 as a sitting president is barred from holding a second consecutive term.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 12-13-05 1222ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020051213e1cd0028p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
